The package binary statically links Rust dependencies. A complete inventory of
the locked Rust package name, version, source checksum, declared license, and
legal-file provenance is installed at
`dependency-licenses/dependency-inventory.json`. Verbatim dependency license,
notice, attribution, and patent files are installed in the content-addressed
`dependency-licenses/rust-license-texts.tar.xz` bundle. The inventory maps each
upstream file to its SHA-256 bundle member.

Direct R dependencies are separately distributed packages rather than bundled
code. Their exact DESCRIPTION roles and version requirements are recorded in
the same inventory; each installed dependency's DESCRIPTION and license files
remain authoritative for its license.

The bundled `extdata/cdf-empty-checkpoint.parquet` asset is copied from
`delta-io/delta-sharing` commit
`4b790695e45bc66a7531f0ddd264725718ee2fcc` (`fake_checkpoint.py`), licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
